# Performance Analysis: RAG Cache Pipeline

## Executive Summary

Based on your constraints (Intel hardware, credit efficiency, 10K+ entries), I'll provide performance budgets and optimization strategies for each component.

---

## 1. EMBEDDING LATENCY

### Performance Budget
- **Target:** < 50ms for embedding generation
- **Current:** ~200-500ms (Python pseudo-embeddings)
- **Target credit impact:** Reduce from 0.81 to 0.30 credits/extraction

### Model Recommendations by Latency

| Model | Size | Intel Latency | Throughput | Memory |
|-------|------|---------------|------------|--------|
| all-MiniLM-L6-v2 | 22MB | **15-25ms** | 40-60 QPS | 120MB |
| Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B | 600M | 80-150ms | 8-12 QPS | 1.2GB |
| BGE-M3 | 568M | 100-180ms | 5-8 QPS | 1.1GB |
| Model2Vec | <1MB | **<1ms** | 1000+ QPS | 50MB |

### Optimization Strategies

**A. Quantize with OpenVINO (Intel-specific)**
```python
# OpenVINO quantization for Intel CPUs
from openvino import Core
from optimum.intel import OVEmbeddingModel

# INT8 quantization: 2-3x speedup on Intel
model = OVEmbeddingModel.from_pretrained(
    "sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2",
    export=True,
    quantize=True
)
```

**B. Batch Processing Pipeline**
```typescript
// src/embedding-pipeline.ts
class EmbeddingPipeline {
  private batchQueue: string[] = [];
  private batchTimer: NodeJS.Timeout | null = null;
  private readonly BATCH_SIZE = 32;
  private readonly BATCH_TIMEOUT_MS = 50;

  async addForEmbedding(text: string): Promise<Float32Array> {
    return new Promise((resolve) => {
      this.batchQueue.push({ text, resolve });

      if (this.batchQueue.length >= this.BATCH_SIZE) {
        this.flushBatch();
      } else if (!this.batchTimer) {
        this.batchTimer = setTimeout(() => this.flushBatch(), this.BATCH_TIMEOUT_MS);
      }
    });
  }
}
```

**C. Async Worker Pool**
```typescript
// Keep embedding generation off main thread
import { Worker } from 'worker_threads';

class EmbeddingWorkerPool {
  private workers: Worker[] = [];
  private queue: PriorityQueue<{ text: string; resolve: Function }>[];

  constructor(poolSize = navigator.hardwareConcurrency || 4) {
    for (let i = 0; i < poolSize; i++) {
      this.workers.push(new Worker('./embedding-worker.js'));
    }
  }
}
```

