## 3. MEMORY USAGE

### Performance Budget
- **Target:** < 500MB total footprint
- **Current:** Unknown (in-memory + Python overhead)

### Memory Breakdown

| Component | Current | Optimized | Strategy |
|-----------|---------|-----------|----------|
| Embedding Model | ~1GB | **150MB** | INT8 quantization |
| Vector Store | 80MB | **150MB** | LanceDB with compression |
| Content Cache | ~500MB | **200MB** | LRU eviction + compression |
| Node.js Process | ~200MB | **150MB** | Stream processing |
| **Total** | ~1.8GB | **450MB** | |

### Optimization: Tiered Memory Architecture

```typescript
// src/cache-tiered.ts
class TieredCache {
  // Hot: L1 (in-memory LRU, 1000 items)
  private l1Cache: Map<string, CachedEntry>;

  // Warm: L2 (SQLite, recent 30 days)
  private l2Store: SQLiteStore;

  // Cold: L3 (compressed archive)
  private l3Archive: CompressedArchive;

  constructor() {
    this.l1Cache = new Map();
    // Limit L1 to 1000 most accessed items
    this.l1Cache.maxSize = 1000;
  }

  async get(key: string): Promise<CachedEntry | null> {
    // L1 check (0.1ms)
    if (this.l1Cache.has(key)) {
      return this.l1Cache.get(key)!;
    }

    // L2 check (2-5ms)
    const l2Entry = await this.l2Store.get(key);
    if (l2Entry) {
      // Promote to L1
      this.l1Cache.set(key, l2Entry);
      return l2Entry;
    }

    // L3 check (10-20ms)
    return this.l3Archive.get(key);
  }
}
```

### Content Compression Strategy

```typescript
// Compress stored content with Brotli
import { brotliCompressSync, brotliDecompressSync } from 'zlib';

class CompressedContentStore {
  async store(content: string, metadata: ContentMetadata) {
    // Brotli: 70-80% compression ratio
    const compressed = brotliCompressSync(Buffer.from(content), {
      params: {
        [zlib.constants.BROTLI_PARAM_QUALITY]: 4,  // Fast compression
        [zlib.constants.BROTLI_PARAM_SIZE_HINT]: content.length
      }
    });

    await this.db.store(compressed, metadata);
  }
}
